# Copy this file to a file named exactly ".env" in the MetaCode folder, next to
# server.js. After editing it, click Settings → "Reload .env" in MetaCode (or
# restart). Settings → AI connection shows which file was read and which
# settings it found. (".env.txt" and files saved by Notepad as "Unicode" work
# too; values here replace same-named variables set in your system.) One KEY=value per line; a value containing # or spaces
# must be in quotes, e.g. REDDIT_CLIENT_SECRET="abc#123" (otherwise everything
# after the # is dropped).

# ── AI (MetaCode's OpenCode service) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Every AI feature goes through MetaCode's own AI service, an OpenCode service
# that runs beside it on this computer (opencode/server.mjs). On a server pm2
# runs it (ecosystem.config.cjs); started with "npm start", MetaCode starts it
# itself. It reads this same file. Full reference: docs/opencode-service.md.
# Keys stay on this computer: they're never sent to the browser, logged or
# returned by an endpoint. After editing, Settings → "Reload .env" reaches the
# service too (with pm2, the OPENCODE_SERVICE_* settings below need a restart
# of both apps).
#
# OpenCode Zen (models offered by the OpenCode team). Works without a key: its
# free models are offered by default, also when the gateway below is set up.
# Free models are rate-limited, and their providers may use prompts to improve
# their models while they're free, so for sensitive posts use paid models or
# the gateway below, and switch the free ones off with
# OPENCODE_DISABLE_FREE_MODELS=1. A key adds the paid models (billed to it):
# sign in at https://opencode.ai/auth, add billing details and create an API
# key.
# OPENCODE_API_KEY=
# OPENCODE_DISABLE_FREE_MODELS=1
#
# The AI gateway (EMIS, OpenAI-compatible). Keys (emis-…) are issued by hand:
# message @kawaii_zxs on Discord (user ID 1079096114273320971) and say what you
# need it for. Each key has a budget — a number of prompts and/or tokens per
# day, week or month; when it runs out the gateway answers 429 until the window
# rolls over. Several keys can be listed, comma-separated; the service rotates
# between them and skips a key whose quota is used up until the gateway says it
# resets.
# EMIS_API_KEY=emis-...
# Its address (this is the default; change it only if you're told to):
# EMIS_BASE_URL=https://emis.zxs-is-very.cool/v1
# Its model list: the gateway's OpenCode config,
# https://emis.zxs-is-very.cool/cli/opencode.json (only models with tool
# calling). Download it again to update the list. Default: emis-models.json in
# the MetaCode folder; without the file the gateway's live list is used.
# EMIS_MODELS_FILE=emis-models.json
# What sends the gateway's non-streamed requests: auto (default) = Python when
# it's installed (with httpx, which comes with the "openai" package in
# requirements.txt, if present), otherwise Node.js; python = always Python;
# node = always Node.js.
# EMIS_PYTHON=… sets the Python command (e.g. py -3).
# EMIS_TRANSPORT=auto
#
# If your network only reaches the internet through a proxy (school or office
# networks), set it here — Node.js doesn't use the system proxy on its own, and
# without it every AI request fails with "Couldn't reach …" (HTTP 502). Used for
# both providers (and MetaCode's other outbound requests; NO_PROXY is honoured);
# EMIS_PROXY=… sets a different one for the gateway only.
# HTTPS_PROXY=http://proxy.example.edu:8080
#
# Optional: the model to use when none is picked in Settings → AI models (or
# the picked one isn't offered), as provider/model: e.g. emis/claude-opus-5.5
# or opencode/big-pickle. Leave empty for Claude Opus 5.5 on the gateway when
# it's set up, otherwise OpenCode Zen's first model: without a Zen key Big
# Pickle; with one the newest release, which can be a free model too, so for
# sensitive posts set OPENCODE_MODEL or OPENCODE_DISABLE_FREE_MODELS=1.
# (EMIS_MODEL=<id>, from earlier versions, still works and means emis/<id>.)
# A reasoning variant goes after # and needs quotes, or it's read as a comment:
# OPENCODE_MODEL="opencode/glm-5.3-flash-free#high"
# OPENCODE_MODEL=
#
# Optional: when the AI service rate-limits a model, MetaCode answers with the
# closest similar model — the same model from the other provider first, then
# the same family and line, nearest version — until it's available again. Set to off to wait
# for the chosen model instead. (Each browser can also turn this off in
# Settings → AI models.) EMIS_MODEL_SWITCH, from earlier versions, still works.
# AI_MODEL_SWITCH=on
# A free model never answers for one that isn't free, so posts meant for the
# gateway's models aren't sent to Zen's free models when its budget is used up.
# on lets free models answer for paid ones too (default off).
# AI_FALLBACK_TO_FREE_MODELS=off
#
# Optional: how long to wait for an AI answer, in milliseconds (1000–600000,
# default 120000). EMIS_TIMEOUT_MS, from earlier versions, still works.
# AI_TIMEOUT_MS=120000
#
# Optional: the most copies of the model AI Coding may run at once (default 16,
# up to 64). Each user picks a number up to this in Settings or on the AI Coding
# page; lower it if your AI key is rate-limited.
# AI_MAX_PARALLEL=16
# When the AI service answers with server errors, AI Coding pauses this long
# first (seconds; doubles with each pause, up to 60).
# AI_BATCH_PAUSE_SECONDS=5
#
# Where the AI service runs (defaults shown; both MetaCode and the service read
# these). It listens on this computer only; keep it that way. A second MetaCode
# copy on the same computer needs its own port here (and, under pm2, its own
# app names).
# OPENCODE_SERVICE_PORT=4097
# OPENCODE_SERVICE_HOST=127.0.0.1
# Its folder for the access token and the model catalog cache:
# OPENCODE_SERVICE_DATA_DIR=opencode-data
# The token MetaCode sends to the service (at least 16 characters). Unset: a
# random one is created in <OPENCODE_SERVICE_DATA_DIR>/token. SECRET.
# OPENCODE_SERVICE_TOKEN=
# auto (default) = MetaCode starts the service itself when nothing answers at
# the default address (OPENCODE_SERVICE_URL unset or that address); off = never
# (pm2 runs it: ecosystem.config.cjs sets this); on = also at another
# OPENCODE_SERVICE_URL on this computer.
# OPENCODE_SERVICE_MANAGED=auto
# The service's address as MetaCode sees it. Unset, or exactly the default
# (http://127.0.0.1:4097/v1, from the host and port above), it is that default
# address. Any other address is a service MetaCode doesn't start (unless
# OPENCODE_SERVICE_MANAGED=on). off switches MetaCode's AI off.
# OPENCODE_SERVICE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4097/v1
#
# More service settings (an extra OpenCode config file, providers to switch
# off, where the model catalog comes from): docs/opencode-service.md.

# Optional, for a server behind a reverse proxy (nginx, Caddy, Cloudflare): the
# public address(es) people open MetaCode at, comma-separated. The Reddit browser's
# WebSocket (/wisp/) is accepted from these even if the proxy rewrites the Host
# header. See docs/deploy-vps.md.
# PUBLIC_URL=https://metac0.de

# Optional: the host name the status page answers on (default status.metac0.de;
# any host starting with "status." works too). Point its DNS at this server.
# STATUS_HOST=status.metac0.de

# ── Server port (default: 3000) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
PORT=3000

# ── Reddit Scraper (sidebar → Scraper) ────────────────────────────────────────
# Full reference: docs/reddit-scraper.md. Needs Node.js 22+.
# Identify your client to Reddit: <platform>:<app id>:<version> (by /u/<username>)
SCRAPER_USER_AGENT=nodejs:metacode-scraper:1.0 (by /u/your_username)

# Optional: Reddit Data API credentials (https://www.reddit.com/prefs/apps,
# app type "script"). Not needed for RedditAPIs.com (the default) or "This
# browser (Scramjet)", where your open MetaCode tab makes the Reddit requests. With them, jobs
# can run on the server through Reddit's official API. The secret stays on this
# server: it is never sent to the browser or to custom scraper code.
# These are the SERVER'S keys, used for jobs from users who haven't added their
# own: everyone without keys shares their Reddit API limit (~100 requests a
# minute). Each user can add their own keys on the Reddit API scraper page →
# Reddit API access; those stay in that user's browser, are sent only with that
# user's jobs and give them their own limit. Server keys can only be set here.
# (A reddit-credentials.json saved by an earlier version is still read.)
REDDIT_CLIENT_ID=
REDDIT_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Optional: RedditAPIs.com key (third-party paid service, not Reddit; billed per
# request). Get one at https://www.redditapis.com/dashboard/api-keys. The
# server's key, for users without their own (each user can add theirs on the
# Reddit API scraper page; it stays in their browser). Never sent to the
# browser or custom code. (A redditapis-key.json from an earlier version is still read.)
REDDITAPIS_KEY=
# REDDITAPIS_BASE_URL=https://api.redditapis.com

# Optional (defaults shown):
# SCRAPER_ENABLED=true
# SCRAPER_RESPECT_ROBOTS_TXT=true
# SCRAPER_MIN_DELAY_MS=1000             minimum gap between requests to one host (all jobs)
# SCRAPER_PUBLIC_MIN_DELAY_MS=6000      minimum gap without API credentials
# SCRAPER_DEFAULT_DELAY_MS=2000
# SCRAPER_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_MS=20000
# SCRAPER_MAX_CONCURRENT_REQUESTS=2
# SCRAPER_MAX_ITEMS=5000
# SCRAPER_MAX_PAGES=50
# SCRAPER_MAX_CONCURRENT_JOBS=2
# SCRAPER_MAX_STORED_JOBS=50
# SCRAPER_JOB_RETENTION_MINUTES=120
# SCRAPER_MAX_RESPONSE_BYTES=8388608
# SCRAPER_CUSTOM_CODE_ENABLED=true
# SCRAPER_CUSTOM_TIMEOUT_MS=120000
# SCRAPER_CUSTOM_MEMORY_MB=64
# SCRAPER_BROWSER_ENABLED=true          in-app Reddit browser (Scramjet)
# SCRAPER_DEFAULT_ENGINE=redditapis     what "Fetch Reddit through" starts on: redditapis | browser | server
#                                       (each browser remembers its own choice)
# SCRAPER_SERVER_TRANSPORT=auto         server HTTPS: python | epoxy | auto (Python if found)
# SCRAPER_PYTHON=python3                Python command for the server engine and the AI Scraper's agent
# SCRAPER_CUSTOM_PYTHON_MEMORY_MB=256   memory limit of Python custom scrapers (Pyodide)
#
# Durable jobs (docs/scraper-network.md): kept on disk and resumed after a restart
# SCRAPER_PERSIST_JOBS=true
# SCRAPER_DATA_DIR=scraper-data
# SCRAPER_MAX_QUEUED_JOBS=20            jobs waiting to start, server-wide (more → "queue full", try later)
# SCRAPER_MAX_DISK_MB=2048
# SCRAPER_PAUSED_RETENTION_HOURS=24     paused jobs left alone this long are cancelled
# SCRAPER_MAX_JOB_WAITS=6               automatic retries after temporary failures (then the job pauses)
# SCRAPER_MAX_JOB_WAIT_MINUTES=30
#
# Network route (administrators only; docs/scraper-network.md). Default: this
# server's own connection. A proxy or a separately managed VPN gateway that
# exposes an HTTP proxy can be used instead. Never routes around blocks or rate
# limits: an access denial stops the job, and failover (off by default) only
# happens while a route itself is down. These URLs may hold credentials: SECRET.
# A ready-made gateway (gluetun + Mullvad in a container): deploy/vpn-gateway/ —
# its setup.sh prints these lines. A configured gateway (or proxy) is used by
# default; SCRAPER_NETWORK_PROVIDERS only changes the order.
# SCRAPER_NETWORK_PROVIDERS=            e.g. vpn-gateway,direct (in order of preference)
# SCRAPER_NETWORK_FAILOVER=off
# SCRAPER_PROXY_URL=http://user:password@proxy.internal:3128  # placeholder (trufflehog:ignore)
# SCRAPER_VPN_GATEWAY_PROXY_URL=http://metacode:password@127.0.0.1:8888  # placeholder (trufflehog:ignore)
# SCRAPER_VPN_GATEWAY_HEALTH_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000/v1/vpn/status
# SCRAPER_VPN_GATEWAY_IP_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000/v1/publicip/ip      shows the exit address
# SCRAPER_VPN_GATEWAY_HEALTH_API_KEY=   SECRET: gluetun's control-server API key (X-API-Key)
# SCRAPER_CIRCUIT_FAILURES=5            route failures in a row that pause requests…
# SCRAPER_CIRCUIT_COOLDOWN_SECONDS=30   …for this long (doubling up to the maximum)
# SCRAPER_CIRCUIT_MAX_COOLDOWN_SECONDS=300
#
# Testing only — point the scraper at a local mock instead of Reddit:
# REDDIT_BASE_URL=https://www.reddit.com
# REDDIT_OAUTH_BASE_URL=https://oauth.reddit.com
# SCRAPER_ALLOW_PRIVATE_NETWORK=false

# ── Accounts and plans (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# With both Supabase values set, people sign in (Supabase Auth), their work is
# saved to their account, and plans and limits apply (public/js/plans.js). Leave
# them unset for a MetaCode without accounts, plans or limits (as before).
# Setup — the database table, Auth URLs, Stripe products and webhook: docs/accounts.md
#
# The project's address and its PUBLISHABLE key (Project Settings → API Keys).
# The publishable key is meant for browsers; never put the secret / service_role
# key here (MetaCode refuses it, because this value is sent to browsers).
# SUPABASE_URL=https://rebxueqhguxicpazvjdv.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_...
#
# Stripe (plans). Without STRIPE_SECRET_KEY everyone signed in is on Free.
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_live_...           (or sk_test_… while testing; a restricted rk_ key works)
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_...         (Developers → Webhooks → your endpoint → Signing secret)
# The products for each plan (these are the defaults) and, optionally, the price
# to sell (default: each product's default price):
# STRIPE_PRODUCT_PRO=prod_VQeJh2lPqfmae9
# STRIPE_PRODUCT_MAX=prod_VQeK26tKchu1VI
# STRIPE_PRODUCT_ULTRA=prod_VQeKXAJtQQLKqm
# STRIPE_PRICE_PRO=price_...
#
# Accounts whose plan you set yourself (staff, testers): a Supabase user id or a
# verified email, = free | pro | max | ultra. Comma-separated.
# ACCOUNT_PLAN_OVERRIDES=you@example.edu=ultra
#
# This server's administrators (verified emails, comma-separated): they see the
# scraper's network diagnostics and queue health. It grants no plan and no
# access to other people's data.
# ADMIN_EMAILS=you@example.edu
#
# Where usage counters and Stripe customer links are kept (JSON; default account-data/)
# ACCOUNT_DATA_DIR=account-data
# PUBLIC_URL (above) is also used for Stripe's return links when set.

# ── Scraper: YouTube, X and LinkedIn (docs/platforms.md) ──────────────────────
# Official APIs only. Users can also add their own key/token on the Scraper page
# (kept in their browser, never stored on the server). All three are SECRET.
# YOUTUBE_API_KEY=                      Google Cloud → enable YouTube Data API v3 → Credentials → API key
# YOUTUBE_DAILY_QUOTA=10000             the key's daily quota (MetaCode meters the server key per Pacific-time day)
# YOUTUBE_ENABLED=true
# X_BEARER_TOKEN=                       developer.x.com → your App → Keys and tokens (reading needs a plan with search)
# X_ENABLED=true
# LINKEDIN_ACCESS_TOKEN=                LinkedIn Developer Portal → an app with the Community Management API →
#                                       OAuth Token Tools → Create token (r_organization… scopes; lasts 60 days).
#                                       Reads the Pages that token's member manages. Archive imports need none.
# LINKEDIN_API_VERSION=                 YYYYMM; empty = last month's, stepping back if LinkedIn doesn't serve it
# LINKEDIN_ENABLED=true

# ── MetaCode Sheets, the desktop app (desktop/, docs/desktop/) ─────────────────
# Part of the Pro, Max and Ultra plans (public/js/plans.js, feature "desktop").
# The app signs in with the same Supabase account and the server checks the
# plan in Stripe, as for the website; it needs accounts turned on (above).
# DESKTOP_ENABLED=true
# How long the app may run offline after its last successful check (hours, 1–336)
# DESKTOP_OFFLINE_HOURS=72
# The key that signs the app's offline leases (Ed25519, PEM; \n for line breaks).
# Unset: one is generated on first use and kept in ACCOUNT_DATA_DIR/desktop-lease-key.pem.
# Release builds can pin its public key (desktop/app-config.json → leasePublicKeys). SECRET.
# DESKTOP_LEASE_PRIVATE_KEY=
# Downloads on the website (/download, desktop-api/downloads.js): the installers of
# the newest *published* GitHub release tagged desktop-v<version> in this repository
# (drafts and pre-releases are never offered). "off" turns the download page's files off.
# DESKTOP_RELEASES_REPO=kevinbwrightgmu/metacode
# Optional: only raises GitHub's API rate limit for the release lookup (a token with no
# extra permissions is enough for a public repository). Sent only to the GitHub API. SECRET.
# DESKTOP_GITHUB_TOKEN=
# Optional: serve the installers from a folder on this server instead of GitHub
# (file names as built: MetaCode-Sheets-<version>-win-x64.exe …; the newest version wins)
# DESKTOP_DOWNLOADS_DIR=
# Where an outdated app's "Download the new version" goes (https://…; default: this site's /download)
# DESKTOP_DOWNLOAD_URL=
# Oldest app version this server accepts (e.g. 1.0.0); older ones are asked to update
# DESKTOP_MIN_VERSION=
# Offer "email me a sign-in link" in the app (for accounts without a password). Only
# turn on after adding metacode-sheets://auth-callback to Supabase → Authentication →
# URL Configuration → Redirect URLs; otherwise the link would open the website instead.
# DESKTOP_EMAIL_LINK=false
# Private single-user servers only: let the app in without accounts (anyone who can
# reach this server could then use the app and its AI quota)
# DESKTOP_WITHOUT_ACCOUNTS=false

# ── AI Coding Lab (Ultra; /ultra/ai-lab) ──────────────────────────────────────
# Coding assistants, project knowledge, datasets and evaluations for Ultra
# subscribers. Access is decided on the server from the billing system; with
# accounts off the Lab stays closed. See docs/ai-lab.md.
# AI_LAB_ENABLED=true
# Where projects, profiles, documents, datasets, runs and audit logs are kept
# (JSON files, one folder per account; default lab-data/)
# AI_LAB_DATA_DIR=lab-data
# Only for a private, single-user install without accounts (everyone who can
# reach the server would share one Lab):
# AI_LAB_WITHOUT_ACCOUNTS=false
# Context budget for models whose context window isn't known (tokens)
# AI_LAB_DEFAULT_CONTEXT_TOKENS=16000
# Knowledge documents: largest file (KB) and documents per project
# AI_LAB_MAX_DOC_KB=1024
# AI_LAB_MAX_DOCS_PER_PROJECT=200
# Evaluation runs at once, across the whole server
# AI_LAB_MAX_RUNNING_EVALS=2
# Price list for cost ESTIMATES (JSON, docs/ai-lab.md). Without one, costs show as unknown.
# AI_LAB_PRICING_FILE=ai-lab-pricing.json
# Code Experiments: coding rules for a Codebook variable run ONLY in the isolated
# sandbox (WebAssembly engine in a locked-down process; plus a network namespace
# and CPU limits where the host allows them — docs/ai-lab.md §8, §14). Workbench and
# evaluation answers are never run. "off" turns all code execution off.
# AI_LAB_CODE_EXECUTION=sandbox
# auto | namespace (refuse runs without an OS network namespace) | process
# AI_LAB_SANDBOX_ISOLATION=auto
# Per run: time (ms), memory (MB, JavaScript / Python), results + logs (KB)
# AI_LAB_SANDBOX_TIMEOUT_MS=15000
# AI_LAB_SANDBOX_MEMORY_MB=64
# AI_LAB_SANDBOX_PYTHON_MEMORY_MB=256
# AI_LAB_SANDBOX_MAX_OUTPUT_KB=8192
# Code experiment runs at once, across the whole server
# AI_LAB_MAX_RUNNING_EXECUTIONS=2
#
# Optional second provider: OpenAI or an OpenAI-compatible API. Answers through
# it are billed to this key by the provider.
# AI_LAB_OPENAI_API_KEY=            # SECRET — never commit it
# AI_LAB_OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
# AI_LAB_OPENAI_MODELS=             # comma list to offer (default: the provider's /models list)
# Fine-tuning through that provider (off by default; it is paid, per trained token):
# AI_LAB_FINE_TUNING=off
# AI_LAB_FINE_TUNE_MODELS=          # base models the provider allows fine-tuning for (check its docs)

# ── Survey Studio ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Folder for surveys, published versions, responses and the shared library
# (JSON files). Relative paths are resolved from where the server starts.
# SURVEY_DATA_DIR=survey-data

# Behind a reverse proxy (nginx, Caddy, Cloudflare, a load balancer): which proxy
# to believe for the visitor's IP address (rate limits, and the respondent IP when
# a survey collects it). A hop count (1 = one proxy in front), "loopback" (a
# proxy on this machine), or a comma-separated list of proxy addresses / CIDR
# ranges. Leave unset when MetaCode is reached directly — forwarded headers are
# then ignored, since anyone could send them.
# TRUST_PROXY=1

# Where the proxy puts the visitor's approximate location, for surveys that
# collect country/region: "cloudflare" (CF-IPCountry, and CF-Region with
# Cloudflare's visitor location headers on) or "<country-header>[,<region-header>]",
# e.g. X-Country-Code,X-Region from nginx GeoIP2. Only set it if the proxy
# overwrites these headers on every request. Unset: location isn't recorded.
# SURVEY_GEO_HEADERS=cloudflare

# ── Projects page ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Folder for saved projects (JSON files). Relative paths are resolved from where
# the server starts.
# PROJECT_DATA_DIR=project-data

# ── Shared projects (needs accounts) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Folder for shared projects, their members, invitations and chat (JSON files,
# readable only by the server's user). Back it up like SURVEY_DATA_DIR. See
# docs/collaboration.md.
# COLLAB_DATA_DIR=collab-data
